<title>GERMANY: TABLE-E. German June ind orders fall 3.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>TABLE-E. German June ind orders fall 3.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS    June 97     May 97    June 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -3.2	 +2.6	 +4.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+1.6	 +9.6	+20.0</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		150.5	155.5	148.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data. @</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				 June 97    May 97   June 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     -3.1	+5.7	166.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison May/Jun 97 with Mar/Apr 97:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +2.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison May/June 97 with May/June 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +5.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +28.9</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +19.1</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -10.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +3.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
